      "text": "In 1945, Australia became a founding member of the United Nations, playing a significant role in the drafting of the UN Charter.",
      "date": "1945"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Referendum on Aboriginal Rights",
      "text": "On 27 May 1967, a referendum was held in which over 90% of Australians voted to include Aboriginal people in the census and allow the federal government to create laws for them.",
      "date": "1967-05-27"
