      "headline": "Great Leap Forward",
      "text": "In 1958, the Great Leap Forward was launched by Mao Zedong as an economic and social campaign to rapidly transform China from an agrarian society into a socialist society through rapid industrialization and collectivization. The campaign led to a significant economic breakdown and is associated with a massive famine.",
      "date": "1958"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cultural Revolution",
      "text": "The Cultural Revolution began in 1966, initiated by Mao Zedong to preserve Chinese communism by purging remnants of capitalist and traditional elements from Chinese society. It caused widespread chaos and resulted in significant cultural and social upheaval.",
      "date": "1966"
    },
