      "headline": "Birth of Jeffrey Dahmer",
      "text": "Jeffrey Lionel Dahmer was born on May 21, 1960, in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA.",
      "date": "1960-05-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Known Murder",
      "text": "On June 18, 1978, Dahmer committed his first murder, killing Steven Hicks, a hitchhiker he picked up and brought to his parents' house in Bath, Ohio.",
      "date": "1978-06-18"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Enlistment in the U.S. Army",
      "text": "In January 1979, Dahmer enlisted in the U.S. Army and was stationed in Germany.",
      "date": "1979-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Discharge from the Army",
      "text": "Dahmer was honorably discharged from the Army due to alcohol abuse in March 1981.",
      "date": "1981-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Move to Milwaukee",
      "text": "In 1982, Dahmer moved to Milwaukee, Wisconsin, where he would later commit most of his murders.",
      "date": "1982"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Arrest for Sexual Assault",
      "text": "In September 1986, Dahmer was arrested for indecent exposure at the Wisconsin State Fair Park.",
      "date": "1986-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Murder of Steven Tuomi",
      "text": "On November 20, 1987, Dahmer killed Steven Tuomi at the Ambassador Hotel in Milwaukee.",
      "date": "1987-11-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Arrest and Conviction for Sexual Assault",
      "text": "In January 1989, Dahmer was arrested for sexually assaulting a 13-year-old boy and was convicted in May 1989.",
      "date": "1989-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release from Prison",
      "text": "Dahmer was released from prison in March 1990 after serving a year for the sexual assault conviction.",
      "date": "1990-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Final Murder",
      "text": "On July 19, 1991, Dahmer committed his final murder, killing Joseph Bradehoft.",
      "date": "1991-07-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Arrest and Discovery of Crimes",
      "text": "Dahmer was arrested on July 22, 1991, after one of his intended victims, Tracy Edwards, escaped and led police to Dahmer's apartment, where evidence of his crimes was discovered.",
      "date": "1991-07-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Trial and Conviction",
      "text": "Dahmer's trial began on January 30, 1992, and he was convicted on February 17, 1992, of 15 counts of murder.",
      "date": "1992-02-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sentencing",
      "text": "On February 17, 1992, Dahmer was sentenced to 15 consecutive life terms in prison.",
      "date": "1992-02-17"
