      "headline": "Adoption of the Latin Alphabet",
      "text": "In 1928, Turkey adopted the Latin alphabet, replacing the Arabic script as part of Atatürk's reforms to modernize and secularize the country.",
      "date": "1928"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Women's Suffrage",
      "text": "In 1934, women in Turkey were granted the right to vote and stand for election, marking a significant step in gender equality in the country.",
      "date": "1934"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Turkey Joins NATO",
      "text": "Turkey became a member of the North Atlantic Treaty Organization (NATO) on February 18, 1952, aligning itself with Western powers during the Cold War.",
      "date": "1952-02-18"
    },
