      "headline": "Last Communication",
      "text": "The last voice communication from Flight 370 occurred at 01:19 local time on March 8, 2014, when the crew acknowledged a transition from Malaysian to Vietnamese air traffic control.",
      "date": "2014-03-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Disappearance from Radar",
      "text": "Flight 370 disappeared from air traffic control radar screens at 01:21 local time on March 8, 2014, while over the South China Sea.",
      "date": "2014-03-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Search and Rescue Operations Begin",
      "text": "Search and rescue operations were initiated on March 8, 2014, after the aircraft was reported missing.",
      "date": "2014-03-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Satellite Data Analysis",
      "text": "On March 15, 2014, it was revealed that satellite data analysis suggested the aircraft had flown for several hours after losing contact, potentially ending in the southern Indian Ocean.",
      "date": "2014-03-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Official Declaration of Loss",
      "text": "On March 24, 2014, Malaysian Prime Minister Najib Razak announced that Flight 370 was assumed to have ended in the southern Indian Ocean, with no survivors.",
      "date": "2014-03-24"
    },
