      "text": "During the late 1970s and early 1980s, AI research faced a period of reduced funding and interest, known as the 'AI Winter', due to unmet expectations.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Deep Blue Defeats Kasparov",
      "text": "In 1997, IBM's Deep Blue became the first computer to defeat a reigning world chess champion, Garry Kasparov, in a match.",
      "date": "1997"
