      "headline": "Operation Reinhard",
      "text": "Beginning in 1942, Operation Reinhard was the code name for the Nazi plan to murder the Jews of the General Government district of occupied Poland, leading to the establishment of extermination camps such as Belzec, Sobibor, and Treblinka.",
      "date": "1942"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Auschwitz-Birkenau Operational",
