      "headline": "Establishes Printing Business",
      "text": "In 1728, Franklin established his own printing business in Philadelphia.",
      "date": "1728"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publishes Poor Richard's Almanack",
      "text": "In 1732, Franklin began publishing 'Poor Richard's Almanack', which became very popular.",
      "date": "1732"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Founds the American Philosophical Society",
      "text": "In 1743, Franklin founded the American Philosophical Society, promoting scientific and intellectual exchange.",
      "date": "1743"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Experiments with Electricity",
      "text": "In 1752, Franklin conducted his famous kite experiment, proving that lightning is a form of electricity.",
      "date": "1752"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Appointed Postmaster of Philadelphia",
      "text": "In 1737, Franklin was appointed postmaster of Philadelphia, which helped him improve the postal system.",
      "date": "1737"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Appointed Deputy Postmaster General for North America",
      "text": "In 1753, Franklin was appointed Deputy Postmaster General for the British colonies in North America.",
      "date": "1753"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Drafts Albany Plan of Union",
      "text": "In 1754, Franklin proposed the Albany Plan of Union, an early attempt to unify the American colonies.",
      "date": "1754"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Serves as Colonial Agent in London",
      "text": "From 1757 to 1775, Franklin served as a colonial agent in London, representing several American colonies.",
      "date": "1757"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Signs the Declaration of Independence",
      "text": "On July 4, 1776, Franklin was one of the signers of the Declaration of Independence.",
      "date": "1776-07-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Appointed Minister to France",
      "text": "In 1778, Franklin was appointed as the United States Minister to France, playing a crucial role in securing French support during the American Revolution.",
      "date": "1778"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Signs Treaty of Paris",
      "text": "In 1783, Franklin was one of the American negotiators who signed the Treaty of Paris, ending the American Revolutionary War.",
