      "headline": "Six-Day War",
      "text": "From June 5 to June 10, 1967, Israel fought against Egypt, Jordan, and Syria, resulting in Israeli control over the West Bank, Gaza Strip, Sinai Peninsula, and Golan Heights.",
      "date": "1967-06-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Yom Kippur War",
      "text": "On October 6, 1973, Egypt and Syria launched a surprise attack on Israel on Yom Kippur, leading to a war that lasted until October 25, 1973.",
      "date": "1973-10-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Camp David Accords",
      "text": "In September 1978, the Camp David Accords were signed by Egypt and Israel, leading to the Egypt-Israel Peace Treaty in 1979.",
      "date": "1978-09"
    },
    {
