      "date": "1937-04-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Joins Ba'ath Party",
      "text": "In 1957, Saddam Hussein joined the Arab Socialist Ba'ath Party, which advocated for Arab nationalism and socialism.",
      "date": "1957"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Attempted Assassination of Qasim",
      "text": "On October 7, 1959, Saddam Hussein participated in an unsuccessful attempt to assassinate Iraqi Prime Minister Abd al-Karim Qasim.",
      "date": "1959-10-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exile in Egypt",
      "text": "Following the failed assassination attempt, Saddam fled to Egypt, where he lived in exile from 1959 to 1963.",
      "date": "1959"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return to Iraq",
      "text": "Saddam returned to Iraq in 1963 after the Ba'ath Party briefly took power in a coup.",
      "date": "1963"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rise to Power",
      "text": "In July 1968, Saddam played a key role in the Ba'ath Party's coup that brought them to power in Iraq. He became the Vice President under President Ahmed Hassan al-Bakr.",
      "date": "1968-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Becomes President of Iraq",
      "text": "On July 16, 1979, Saddam Hussein became the President of Iraq after forcing President Ahmed Hassan al-Bakr to resign.",
      "date": "1979-07-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Iran-Iraq War",
      "text": "The Iran-Iraq War began on September 22, 1980, when Iraq invaded Iran. The conflict lasted until 1988.",
      "date": "1980-09-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Anfal Campaign",
      "text": "From 1986 to 1989, Saddam's regime conducted the Anfal campaign against the Kurdish population in northern Iraq, resulting in mass casualties and destruction.",
      "date": "1986"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Invasion of Kuwait",
      "text": "On August 2, 1990, Iraq invaded Kuwait, leading to the Gulf War after a coalition led by the United States intervened.",
      "date": "1990-08-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Gulf War",
      "text": "The Gulf War began on January 17, 1991, when coalition forces launched Operation Desert Storm to liberate Kuwait from Iraqi occupation.",
      "date": "1991-01-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Re-election as President",
      "text": "In 1995, Saddam Hussein was re-elected as President of Iraq in a referendum, claiming a 99.96% approval rate.",
      "date": "1995"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Overthrown in Iraq War",
      "text": "On March 20, 2003, the Iraq War began with a U.S.-led invasion, leading to the overthrow of Saddam Hussein's regime.",
      "date": "2003-03-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Capture by U.S. Forces",
      "text": "Saddam Hussein was captured by U.S. forces on December 13, 2003, near Tikrit, Iraq.",
      "date": "2003-12-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Trial and Execution",
      "text": "Saddam Hussein was tried and found guilty of crimes against humanity. He was executed by hanging on December 30, 2006.",
      "date": "2006-12-30"
    }
  ]
}

