    },
    {
      "headline": "First Broadcast",
      "text": "The first broadcast of the Voice of Vietnam took place on September 7, 1945, from Hanoi. This marked the beginning of VOV's role in disseminating information and promoting the policies of the Communist Party and the laws of the state.",
      "date": "1945-09-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion During the Vietnam War",
      "text": "During the Vietnam War, VOV expanded its operations to include broadcasts in multiple languages, aiming to reach international audiences and promote the Vietnamese government's perspective.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Post-War Development",
      "text": "After the Vietnam War ended in 1975, VOV continued to develop its broadcasting capabilities, expanding its reach and modernizing its technology to better serve the reunified Vietnam.",
      "date": "1975"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of FM Broadcasting",
      "text": "In the 1990s, VOV introduced FM broadcasting, which improved the quality of its radio transmissions and allowed for a wider range of programming.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
