      "text": "In 1936, Unit 731 was established as a covert biological and chemical warfare research and development unit of the Imperial Japanese Army. It was based in the Pingfang district of Harbin, in the Japanese puppet state of Manchukuo.",
      "date": "1936"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Beginning of Human Experimentation",
      "text": "Unit 731 began conducting lethal human experimentation and biological weapons manufacturing during the Second Sino-Japanese War, which started in 1937.",
      "date": "1937"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion During World War II",
      "text": "During World War II, Unit 731 expanded its operations, establishing branch offices throughout China and Southeast Asia. The unit was responsible for numerous atrocities, including the deaths of thousands of people due to human experimentation and biological warfare.",
      "date": "1939"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Unit 731's Operations",
      "text": "In 1945, with the end of World War II, Unit 731 ceased its operations. The unit's activities were later investigated, but many of those involved were not prosecuted due to a deal with the United States for the exchange of research data.",
      "date": "1945"
    }
  ]
}

