      "text": "The Ghaznavid Empire, with its capital in Ghazni, was established in 977 CE.",
      "date": "0977"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mughal Empire Control",
      "text": "The Mughal Empire controlled parts of Afghanistan starting in 1526.",
      "date": "1526"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Durrani Empire Foundation",
      "text": "In 1747, Ahmad Shah Durrani founded the Durrani Empire, often considered the foundation of modern Afghanistan.",
      "date": "1747"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Anglo-Afghan War",
      "text": "The First Anglo-Afghan War took place from 1839 to 1842, resulting in a temporary British occupation.",
      "date": "1839"
    },
