    {
      "headline": "Copa América Becomes Official",
      "text": "In 1917, the tournament was officially recognized by CONMEBOL, the South American football confederation, and continued to be held annually.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the Trophy",
      "text": "The Copa América trophy was introduced in 1917, awarded to the tournament's winning team.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Tournament Outside Argentina",
      "text": "The 1919 Copa América was held in Brazil, marking the first time the tournament was hosted outside Argentina.",
