      "headline": "Greenland Becomes Part of Norway",
      "text": "In 1261, Greenland became part of the Kingdom of Norway.",
      "date": "1261"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Union with Denmark",
      "text": "In 1380, Norway entered into a union with Denmark, and Greenland became part of this union.",
      "date": "1380"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Recolonization by Denmark",
      "text": "In 1721, Denmark began recolonizing Greenland, starting with a mission led by Hans Egede.",
      "date": "1721"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Greenland Becomes a Danish Colony",
      "text": "In 1814, following the Treaty of Kiel, Greenland was formally recognized as a Danish colony.",
      "date": "1814"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Greenland Gains Home Rule",
      "text": "Greenland was granted home rule on May 1, 1979, allowing for greater autonomy from Denmark.",
      "date": "1979-05-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Self-Government Act",
      "text": "On June 21, 2009, Greenland assumed self-government with the Self-Government Act, further expanding its autonomy.",
