      "text": "On October 28, 1492, Christopher Columbus arrived in Cuba during his first voyage to the Americas, claiming the island for Spain.",
      "date": "1492-10-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Spanish Colonization",
      "text": "In 1511, Diego Velázquez de Cuéllar began the Spanish conquest of Cuba, establishing the first Spanish settlement at Baracoa.",
      "date": "1511"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Havana Founded",
      "text": "Havana was founded by the Spanish on August 25, 1515, and later became the capital of Cuba.",
      "date": "1515-08-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ten Years' War",
      "text": "The Ten Years' War, the first of three wars for Cuban independence from Spain, began on October 10, 1868.",
      "date": "1868-10-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Spanish Rule",
      "text": "The Spanish-American War ended in 1898, resulting in Spain relinquishing control of Cuba to the United States.",
      "date": "1898"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cuban Independence",
      "text": "Cuba gained formal independence from the United States on May 20, 1902, becoming the Republic of Cuba.",
      "date": "1902-05-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cuban Revolution",
      "text": "The Cuban Revolution, led by Fidel Castro, culminated in the overthrow of the Batista government on January 1, 1959.",
      "date": "1959-01-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bay of Pigs Invasion",
      "text": "The Bay of Pigs Invasion, a failed military invasion of Cuba by Cuban exiles sponsored by the U.S. government, occurred in April 1961.",
      "date": "1961-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cuban Missile Crisis",
      "text": "In October 1962, the Cuban Missile Crisis occurred, a 13-day confrontation between the United States and the Soviet Union over Soviet ballistic missiles deployed in Cuba.",
      "date": "1962-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Soviet Support",
      "text": "In 1991, the dissolution of the Soviet Union led to the end of Soviet economic support for Cuba, resulting in a severe economic crisis known as the Special Period.",
      "date": "1991"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Raúl Castro Becomes President",
      "text": "Raúl Castro officially became the President of Cuba on February 24, 2008, succeeding his brother Fidel Castro.",
      "date": "2008-02-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Restoration of U.S.-Cuba Relations",
      "text": "On December 17, 2014, the United States and Cuba announced the restoration of diplomatic relations, ending a 54-year stretch of hostility.",
      "date": "2014-12-17"
    }
  ]
}

