      "text": "Jury selection for the trial began on September 26, 1994.",
      "date": "1994-09-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Trial Begins",
      "text": "The trial of O.J. Simpson began on January 24, 1995, in Los Angeles County Superior Court.",
      "date": "1995-01-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Opening Statements",
      "text": "Opening statements in the trial were made on January 24, 1995.",
      "date": "1995-01-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The Glove Demonstration",
      "text": "On June 15, 1995, O.J. Simpson tried on a pair of gloves found at the crime scene, which appeared not to fit him, leading to the famous phrase by defense attorney Johnnie Cochran: 'If it doesn't fit, you must acquit.'",
      "date": "1995-06-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Closing Arguments",
      "text": "Closing arguments in the trial were presented on September 27, 1995.",
      "date": "1995-09-27"
    },
