      "text": "On March 3, 1918, Lenin's government signed the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk, ending Russia's involvement in World War I.",
      "date": "1918-03-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Russian Civil War",
      "text": "From 1917 to 1922, Lenin's government fought and won the Russian Civil War, consolidating Bolshevik power.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the Soviet Union",
      "text": "On December 30, 1922, Lenin played a key role in the formation of the Soviet Union, uniting multiple Soviet republics under a federal government.",
      "date": "1922-12-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lenin's Death",
      "text": "Vladimir Lenin died on January 21, 1924, in Gorki, Soviet Union, after suffering a series of strokes.",
