      "headline": "Resignation from the Army",
      "text": "Grant resigned from the U.S. Army on July 31, 1854, amid allegations of drinking problems.",
      "date": "1854-07-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rejoining the Army",
      "text": "Grant rejoined the U.S. Army in 1861 at the outbreak of the American Civil War, initially serving as a colonel.",
      "date": "1861"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Fort Donelson",
      "text": "Grant captured Fort Donelson in Tennessee on February 16, 1862, earning the nickname 'Unconditional Surrender' Grant.",
      "date": "1862-02-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Promotion to Major General",
      "text": "Grant was promoted to major general of volunteers on February 16, 1862, following his success at Fort Donelson.",
      "date": "1862-02-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Shiloh",
      "text": "Grant led Union forces to a costly victory at the Battle of Shiloh on April 6-7, 1862.",
      "date": "1862-04-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Siege of Vicksburg",
      "text": "Grant successfully led the Union Army in the Siege of Vicksburg, culminating in the city's surrender on July 4, 1863.",
      "date": "1863-07-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Promotion to Lieutenant General",
      "text": "Grant was promoted to lieutenant general on March 9, 1864, giving him command of all Union armies.",
      "date": "1864-03-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Surrender at Appomattox",
      "text": "On April 9, 1865, Confederate General Robert E. Lee surrendered to Grant at Appomattox Court House, effectively ending the Civil War.",
      "date": "1865-04-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Inauguration as President",
      "text": "Ulysses S. Grant was inaugurated as the 18th President of the United States on March 4, 1869.",
      "date": "1869-03-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Re-election as President",
      "text": "Grant was re-elected for a second term as President of the United States in 1872.",
      "date": "1872"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Presidency",
      "text": "Grant's presidency ended on March 4, 1877, after serving two terms.",
      "date": "1877-03-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World Tour",
      "text": "Grant embarked on a world tour from 1877 to 1879, visiting Europe, the Middle East, and Asia.",
      "date": "1877"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of Memoirs",
      "text": "Grant completed his memoirs shortly before his death, which were published in 1885 and became a critical and financial success.",
      "date": "1885"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Ulysses S. Grant",
      "text": "Ulysses S. Grant died on July 23, 1885, at Mount McGregor, New York, after battling throat cancer.",
