      "text": "Mary I was born on February 18, 1516, at the Palace of Placentia in Greenwich, England.",
      "date": "1516-02-18"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mary Becomes Princess of Wales",
      "text": "In 1525, Mary was given her own court at Ludlow Castle and was referred to as the Princess of Wales, although she was never formally invested with the title.",
      "date": "1525"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mary Declared Illegitimate",
      "text": "In 1533, following the annulment of her parents' marriage, Mary was declared illegitimate and removed from the line of succession.",
      "date": "1533"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Restoration to Succession",
      "text": "In 1544, the Third Succession Act restored Mary to the line of succession after her half-brother Edward VI.",
      "date": "1544"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mary Becomes Queen of England",
      "text": "Mary I became Queen of England on July 19, 1553, following the death of her half-brother Edward VI and the brief reign of Lady Jane Grey.",
      "date": "1553-07-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Marriage to Philip II of Spain",
      "text": "Mary married Philip II of Spain on July 25, 1554, at Winchester Cathedral.",
      "date": "1554-07-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mary's Reign Begins",
      "text": "Mary's reign officially began on October 1, 1553, with her coronation at Westminster Abbey.",
      "date": "1553-10-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Marian Persecutions",
      "text": "Between 1555 and 1558, Mary I ordered the execution of over 280 religious dissenters, earning her the nickname 'Bloody Mary'.",
      "date": "1555"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Loss of Calais",
      "text": "In January 1558, England lost Calais, its last possession in France, which was a significant blow to Mary's reign.",
      "date": "1558-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Mary I",
      "text": "Mary I died on November 17, 1558, at St James's Palace in London. She was succeeded by her half-sister Elizabeth I.",
      "date": "1558-11-17"
    }
  ]
}

