      "text": "Julian Paul Assange was born on July 3, 1971, in Townsville, Queensland, Australia.",
      "date": "1971-07-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Founding of WikiLeaks",
      "text": "In 2006, Julian Assange founded WikiLeaks, an international non-profit organization that publishes news leaks and classified media provided by anonymous sources.",
      "date": "2006"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of Collateral Murder Video",
      "text": "On April 5, 2010, WikiLeaks released the Collateral Murder video, showing a U.S. helicopter attack in Baghdad that killed several people, including two Reuters journalists.",
      "date": "2010-04-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of Afghan War Logs",
      "text": "On July 25, 2010, WikiLeaks published the Afghan War Logs, a collection of over 75,000 classified documents about the war in Afghanistan.",
      "date": "2010-07-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of Iraq War Logs",
      "text": "On October 22, 2010, WikiLeaks released the Iraq War Logs, consisting of nearly 400,000 classified U.S. military documents detailing the Iraq War.",
      "date": "2010-10-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of U.S. Diplomatic Cables",
      "text": "On November 28, 2010, WikiLeaks began releasing U.S. diplomatic cables, a collection of more than 250,000 diplomatic cables from U.S. embassies around the world.",
      "date": "2010-11-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Arrest in the United Kingdom",
      "text": "On December 7, 2010, Julian Assange was arrested in the United Kingdom under a European Arrest Warrant issued by Sweden for questioning on allegations of sexual misconduct.",
      "date": "2010-12-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Asylum in the Ecuadorian Embassy",
      "text": "On June 19, 2012, Julian Assange sought asylum in the Ecuadorian Embassy in London to avoid extradition to Sweden, where he was wanted for questioning.",
      "date": "2012-06-19"
    },
