      "text": "The QR code was invented in 1994 by the Japanese company Denso Wave, a subsidiary of the Toyota Group. It was developed to track automobile parts during manufacturing.",
      "date": "1994"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of QR Code Standard",
      "text": "In 1997, Denso Wave released the QR code as an open standard, allowing anyone to use the technology without paying licensing fees.",
      "date": "1997"
    },
    {
      "headline": "ISO Standardization",
      "text": "In 2000, the QR code was standardized as ISO/IEC 18004, making it an internationally recognized standard for two-dimensional barcodes.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "QR Code Usage in Mobile Phones",
      "text": "The widespread adoption of smartphones in the late 2000s led to increased use of QR codes for various applications, including marketing, ticketing, and payments.",
      "date": "2000s"
    },
