      "text": "In 1898, the Bombay City Improvement Trust was established to improve the living conditions in the city.",
      "date": "1898"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bombay Presidency Reforms",
      "text": "In 1906, the Bombay Municipal Corporation Act was passed, giving more power to the local government.",
      "date": "1906"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bombay Presidency Reforms",
      "text": "In 1911, the Gateway of India was built to commemorate the visit of King George V and Queen Mary.",
      "date": "1911"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bombay Presidency Reforms",
      "text": "In 1924, the Bombay Stock Exchange was established, becoming the first stock exchange in India.",
      "date": "1924"
