      "headline": "Birth of Krishna",
      "text": "Krishna was born in the city of Mathura in a prison cell to Devaki and Vasudeva. His birth is celebrated as Krishna Janmashtami, which falls in late August or early September according to the lunisolar Hindu calendar.",
      "date": "-0322"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Krishna's Childhood in Vrindavan",
      "text": "Krishna spent his childhood in the village of Vrindavan, where he was raised by his foster parents, Nanda and Yashoda. During this time, he performed many miraculous feats and played with the gopis (cowherd girls).",
      "date": "-0315"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Krishna's Youth and the Defeat of Kamsa",
      "text": "As a young man, Krishna returned to Mathura and defeated his tyrannical uncle Kamsa, who had usurped the throne from Krishna's grandfather, Ugrasena.",
      "date": "-0310"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Krishna as a Prince of Dwaraka",
      "text": "Krishna established the city of Dwaraka, where he became a prince and ruled over the Yadava clan.",
      "date": "-0305"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Role in the Mahabharata",
      "text": "Krishna played a crucial role in the Mahabharata, serving as a charioteer and advisor to Arjuna. He delivered the Bhagavad Gita, a sacred Hindu scripture, during the Kurukshetra War.",
      "date": "-0300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Krishna's Departure",
      "text": "Krishna departed from the world after being accidentally shot by a hunter named Jara. His departure marks the end of the Dvapara Yuga and the beginning of the Kali Yuga.",
      "date": "-0300"
    }
  ]
}

