      "text": "Machu Picchu was constructed in the mid-15th century, during the reign of the Inca emperor Pachacuti (1438–1472). It is believed to have been built as an estate for him.",
      "date": "1450"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Abandonment of Machu Picchu",
      "text": "Machu Picchu was abandoned in the 16th century, around the time of the Spanish Conquest. The exact date is not known, but it is believed to have been abandoned by the Incas around 1572.",
      "date": "1572"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rediscovery by Hiram Bingham",
      "text": "On July 24, 1911, American historian and explorer Hiram Bingham rediscovered Machu Picchu with the help of local indigenous farmers. This brought international attention to the site.",
      "date": "1911-07-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Machu Picchu Declared a Peruvian Historical Sanctuary",
      "text": "In 1981, Machu Picchu was declared a Peruvian Historical Sanctuary, recognizing its cultural and historical significance.",
      "date": "1981"
    },
    {
      "headline": "UNESCO World Heritage Site Designation",
      "text": "In 1983, Machu Picchu was designated as a UNESCO World Heritage Site, acknowledging its importance as a cultural and natural heritage site.",
      "date": "1983"
    },
    {
      "headline": "New Seven Wonders of the World",
      "text": "On July 7, 2007, Machu Picchu was voted one of the New Seven Wonders of the World in a worldwide Internet poll.",
