      "text": "The first mention of Montenegro as a distinct region dates back to the 9th century, when it was part of the Byzantine Empire.",
      "date": "0800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the Principality of Duklja",
      "text": "In the late 10th century, the Principality of Duklja was established, which is considered a predecessor state to modern Montenegro.",
      "date": "0990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Independence of Duklja",
      "text": "Duklja gained independence from the Byzantine Empire in 1042 under the leadership of Stefan Vojislav.",
      "date": "1042"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Zeta as a Prominent State",
      "text": "By the 14th century, the region known as Zeta became a prominent state, which is considered a medieval precursor to Montenegro.",
      "date": "1300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ottoman Conquest",
      "text": "In 1496, Montenegro fell under Ottoman rule, although it maintained a degree of autonomy.",
      "date": "1496"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Montenegrin Independence",
      "text": "Montenegro declared independence from the Ottoman Empire in 1878, recognized at the Congress of Berlin.",
      "date": "1878"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Kingdom of Montenegro",
      "text": "In 1910, Montenegro was proclaimed a kingdom under King Nikola I.",
      "date": "1910"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Annexation by Serbia",
      "text": "In 1918, Montenegro was annexed by the Kingdom of Serbia, later becoming part of the Kingdom of Serbs, Croats, and Slovenes.",
      "date": "1918"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World War II and Liberation",
      "text": "During World War II, Montenegro was occupied by Axis forces, but was liberated by Yugoslav Partisans in 1944.",
      "date": "1944"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Republic within Yugoslavia",
      "text": "After World War II, Montenegro became one of the six republics of the Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia.",
      "date": "1945"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Independence Referendum",
      "text": "On May 21, 2006, Montenegro held a referendum on independence from the State Union of Serbia and Montenegro, which passed with 55.5% of the vote.",
      "date": "2006-05-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Declaration of Independence",
      "text": "Montenegro officially declared independence on June 3, 2006.",
      "date": "2006-06-03"
