      "headline": "Emergence of the Sovereign Citizen Movement",
      "text": "The sovereign citizen movement began to appear in the United States in the early 1970s. It is a loose group of anti-government activists, tax protesters, and conspiracy theorists who claim not to be subject to government statutes unless they consent to them.",
      "date": "1970"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion to Other Countries",
      "text": "During the 2000s, a similar movement known as the freeman on the land emerged in Canada. This movement later spread to other Commonwealth countries, including Australia, New Zealand, and the United Kingdom.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "FBI's Classification",
      "text": "The FBI has classified sovereign citizens as 'anti-government extremists' who believe they are separate or 'sovereign' from the United States, despite physically residing in the country.",
      "date": "2010"
    }
  ]
}

