      "text": "Catherine de' Medici was born on April 13, 1519, in Florence, Italy, into the powerful Medici family.",
      "date": "1519-04-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Marriage to Henry, Duke of Orléans",
      "text": "On October 28, 1533, Catherine de' Medici married Henry, Duke of Orléans, who later became King Henry II of France.",
      "date": "1533-10-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Becomes Queen Consort of France",
      "text": "Catherine became Queen Consort of France on July 31, 1547, following the accession of her husband, Henry II, to the throne.",
      "date": "1547-07-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of King Henry II",
      "text": "King Henry II died on July 10, 1559, leaving Catherine as the queen mother with significant influence over her sons' reigns.",
      "date": "1559-07-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of Francis II",
      "text": "Catherine's son, Francis II, became king on July 10, 1559, but his reign was short-lived, ending with his death on December 5, 1560.",
      "date": "1559-07-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of Charles IX",
      "text": "Catherine's second son, Charles IX, ascended to the throne on December 5, 1560. Catherine acted as regent during his minority and continued to wield significant influence throughout his reign.",
      "date": "1560-12-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "St. Bartholomew's Day Massacre",
      "text": "On August 24, 1572, the St. Bartholomew's Day Massacre occurred, a significant event during Charles IX's reign, with Catherine often implicated in its orchestration.",
      "date": "1572-08-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of Henry III",
      "text": "Catherine's third son, Henry III, became king on May 30, 1574, after the death of Charles IX. Catherine continued to play a crucial role in the political affairs of France.",
      "date": "1574-05-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Catherine de' Medici",
      "text": "Catherine de' Medici died on January 5, 1589, at the Château de Blois in France, marking the end of her significant influence in French politics.",
      "date": "1589-01-05"
    }
  ]
}

