      "text": "On June 24, 1821, the Battle of Carabobo took place, which was a decisive victory for the independence forces led by Simón Bolívar, leading to the liberation of Caracas.",
      "date": "1821-06-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Gran Colombia Dissolution",
      "text": "In 1830, Venezuela separated from Gran Colombia, a union that included Colombia, Ecuador, and Panama, becoming an independent republic.",
      "date": "1830"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Discovery of Oil",
      "text": "In 1922, the discovery of the Maracaibo Basin oil fields marked the beginning of Venezuela's transformation into a major oil producer.",
      "date": "1922"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Military Coup",
      "text": "On November 24, 1948, a military coup overthrew the democratically elected government of Rómulo Gallegos.",
      "date": "1948-11-24"
    },
