      "text": "On December 4, 2016, Edgar Maddison Welch entered the Comet Ping Pong pizzeria in Washington, D.C., armed with a rifle, to investigate the Pizzagate conspiracy theory. He fired at least one shot but no one was injured. Welch was arrested and later sentenced to four years in prison.",
      "date": "2016-12-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Discrediting of Pizzagate",
      "text": "By late 2016, Pizzagate had been thoroughly discredited by a wide range of organizations, including law enforcement agencies, fact-checkers, and media outlets. The Washington, D.C. police stated that the theory was false and dangerous.",
      "date": "2016-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Continued Influence of Pizzagate",
      "text": "Despite being debunked, the Pizzagate conspiracy theory continued to influence some online communities and was referenced in subsequent conspiracy theories, including QAnon.",
