      "text": "In October 2020, SpaceX began public beta testing of the Starlink internet service, initially in the United States, under the program name 'Better Than Nothing Beta'.",
      "date": "2020-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Starlink Exceeds 1,000 Satellites",
      "text": "By January 2021, SpaceX had successfully launched over 1,000 Starlink satellites, significantly expanding its internet coverage capabilities.",
      "date": "2021-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Global Coverage Achieved",
      "text": "In September 2021, SpaceX announced that Starlink had achieved global coverage, providing internet service to users in over 100 countries.",
      "date": "2021-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Starlink Provides Service in Ukraine",
      "text": "In February 2022, following the Russian invasion of Ukraine, SpaceX provided Starlink internet service to Ukraine to maintain communication infrastructure.",
