      "text": "In the 19th century, Baphomet resurfaced during debates regarding the suppression of the Templars. Various occult and mystical traditions began to claim Baphomet as a symbol of balance and synthesis, with origins in Gnostic teachings.",
      "date": "1800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Éliphas Lévi's Sabbatic Goat Illustration",
      "text": "In 1856, Éliphas Lévi associated Baphomet with the Sabbatic Goat illustration. This image composed of binary elements represented the 'symbolization of the equilibrium of opposites': both human and animal, both masculine and feminine, combined in metaphysical unity.",
      "date": "1856"
    }
  ]
}

