    },
    {
      "headline": "Counter-Terrorist Operation Regime Introduced",
      "text": "On 10 August 2024, Russian authorities introduced a 'counter-terrorist operation' regime in Kursk, Belgorod, and Bryansk oblasts.",
      "date": "2024-08-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ukrainian Territorial Gains",
      "text": "By the end of the first week of the incursion, the Ukrainian military claimed it had captured 1,000 km² (390 sq mi) of Russian territory, while Russian authorities acknowledged that Ukraine had captured 28 settlements.",
      "date": "2024-08-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of Ukrainian Military Administration",
      "text": "Ukraine established a military administration for the territory under its control on 15 August 2024.",
      "date": "2024-08-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Stalling of Ukrainian Advance",
      "text": "By early October 2024, the advance of Ukraine had stalled.",
      "date": "2024-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Russian Forces Retake Territory",
      "text": "In October and the first half of November 2024, Russian forces retook around half of the territory occupied by Ukraine in its furthest advance during the offensive.",
