      "headline": "Formation of the Livonian Confederation",
      "text": "In 1228, the Livonian Confederation was formed, which included present-day Latvia. It was a loosely organized confederation of territories in the Baltic region.",
      "date": "1228"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Vilnius",
      "text": "In 1561, the Treaty of Vilnius was signed, marking the end of the Livonian War and the incorporation of Latvian territories into the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth.",
      "date": "1561"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Swedish Rule",
      "text": "In 1629, following the Polish-Swedish War, most of Latvia came under Swedish control, marking the beginning of the Swedish rule over the region.",
      "date": "1629"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Russian Empire Annexation",
      "text": "In 1721, after the Great Northern War, Latvia was ceded to the Russian Empire under the Treaty of Nystad.",
      "date": "1721"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Proclamation of Independence",
      "text": "On November 18, 1918, Latvia declared its independence from Russia, establishing the Republic of Latvia.",
      "date": "1918-11-18"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Soviet Occupation",
      "text": "In 1940, Latvia was occupied and annexed by the Soviet Union as part of the Molotov-Ribbentrop Pact.",
      "date": "1940"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nazi Occupation",
      "text": "In 1941, during World War II, Nazi Germany occupied Latvia following Operation Barbarossa.",
      "date": "1941"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reoccupation by the Soviet Union",
      "text": "In 1944, the Soviet Union reoccupied Latvia, and it remained a part of the USSR until 1991.",
      "date": "1944"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Restoration of Independence",
      "text": "On August 21, 1991, Latvia restored its independence following the dissolution of the Soviet Union.",
      "date": "1991-08-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Joining the European Union",
      "text": "On May 1, 2004, Latvia became a member of the European Union.",
      "date": "2004-05-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Adoption of the Euro",
      "text": "On January 1, 2014, Latvia adopted the euro as its official currency, replacing the Latvian lats.",
