      "headline": "Construction of the Great Pyramid of Giza",
      "text": "The Great Pyramid of Giza was constructed around 2580–2560 BC. It is the oldest of the Seven Wonders and the only one to remain largely intact.",
      "date": "-2580"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of the Hanging Gardens of Babylon",
      "text": "The Hanging Gardens of Babylon were said to have been built in the ancient city-state of Babylon, near present-day Hillah, Babil province, in Iraq. The exact date of construction is unknown, but they are often attributed to the reign of Nebuchadnezzar II, who ruled from 605–562 BC.",
      "date": "-0605"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of the Statue of Zeus at Olympia",
      "text": "The Statue of Zeus at Olympia was created by the sculptor Phidias around 435 BC. It was a giant seated figure, about 12 meters tall, made by the Greek sculptor Phidias around 435 BC at the sanctuary of Olympia, Greece.",
      "date": "-0435"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of the Temple of Artemis at Ephesus",
      "text": "The Temple of Artemis at Ephesus was completed around 550 BC. It was a large temple dedicated to the goddess Artemis, located in Ephesus (near the modern town of Selçuk in present-day Turkey).",
      "date": "-0550"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of the Mausoleum at Halicarnassus",
      "text": "The Mausoleum at Halicarnassus was built between 353 and 350 BC. It was a tomb built for Mausolus, a satrap of the Persian Empire, and his sister-wife Artemisia II of Caria.",
      "date": "-0353"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of the Colossus of Rhodes",
      "text": "The Colossus of Rhodes was completed in 280 BC. It was a statue of the sun god Helios, erected in the city of Rhodes, on the Greek island of the same name, by Chares of Lindos.",
      "date": "-0280"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of the Lighthouse of Alexandria",
      "text": "The Lighthouse of Alexandria, also known as the Pharos of Alexandria, was completed in the 3rd century BC, during the reign of Ptolemy II Philadelphus (280–247 BC). It was a tower built by the Ptolemaic Kingdom on the island of Pharos.",
      "date": "-0280"
    }
  ]
}

