      "headline": "Maya Civilization Flourishes",
      "text": "The Maya civilization flourished in the region that is now Belize, with significant developments in architecture, mathematics, and astronomy. This period saw the rise of major city-states such as Caracol, Lamanai, and Xunantunich.",
      "date": "-1500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Spanish Exploration",
      "text": "Spanish explorers arrived in the region in the early 16th century, but they did not establish permanent settlements due to resistance from the Maya and the lack of resources.",
      "date": "1500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "British Settlement Begins",
      "text": "British settlers, known as Baymen, began to establish settlements along the coast of Belize in the 17th century, primarily for logging mahogany and other hardwoods.",
      "date": "1638"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of St. George's Caye",
      "text": "On September 10, 1798, the British Baymen and their allies defeated a Spanish fleet attempting to assert control over the area. This victory is celebrated as a national holiday in Belize.",
      "date": "1798-09-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Belize Becomes British Honduras",
      "text": "In 1862, the settlement became a British Crown Colony known as British Honduras.",
      "date": "1862"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hurricane Hattie",
      "text": "On October 31, 1961, Hurricane Hattie struck Belize City, causing widespread destruction and prompting the government to relocate the capital to Belmopan.",
      "date": "1961-10-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Self-Government Achieved",
      "text": "British Honduras achieved self-government in January 1964, with George Cadle Price as the first Premier.",
      "date": "1964-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Renaming to Belize",
      "text": "In June 1973, the colony was officially renamed Belize.",
      "date": "1973-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Independence from the United Kingdom",
      "text": "Belize gained full independence from the United Kingdom on September 21, 1981, becoming a sovereign nation.",
      "date": "1981-09-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Belize Joins CARICOM",
      "text": "In 1974, Belize became a member of the Caribbean Community (CARICOM), strengthening its ties with other Caribbean nations.",
      "date": "1974"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Belize Joins the United Nations",
      "text": "Belize became a member of the United Nations on September 25, 1981, shortly after gaining independence.",
      "date": "1981-09-25"
    }
  ]
}

