      "text": "According to Jewish tradition, God made a covenant with Abraham, promising him descendants and land. This event is foundational to Judaism and is traditionally dated to around 1812 BCE.",
      "date": "-1812"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exodus from Egypt",
      "text": "The Exodus, the departure of the Israelites from slavery in Egypt under the leadership of Moses, is a central event in Jewish history. It is traditionally dated to around 1446 BCE.",
      "date": "-1446"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Receiving the Torah at Mount Sinai",
      "text": "According to Jewish tradition, Moses received the Torah from God at Mount Sinai, establishing the laws and commandments that form the basis of Judaism. This event is traditionally dated to around 1312 BCE.",
      "date": "-1312"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of the First Temple",
      "text": "King Solomon built the First Temple in Jerusalem, which became the central place of worship for the Jewish people. This event is traditionally dated to around 957 BCE.",
      "date": "-0957"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Destruction of the First Temple",
      "text": "The First Temple was destroyed by the Babylonians under King Nebuchadnezzar II in 586 BCE, leading to the Babylonian Exile.",
      "date": "-0586"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return from Babylonian Exile",
      "text": "Following the decree of Cyrus the Great, the Jewish people returned from Babylonian exile and began rebuilding the Temple in Jerusalem. This event is traditionally dated to 538 BCE.",
      "date": "-0538"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of the Second Temple",
      "text": "The Second Temple was completed in 516 BCE, restoring the central place of worship for the Jewish people in Jerusalem.",
      "date": "-0516"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Maccabean Revolt",
      "text": "The Maccabean Revolt against the Seleucid Empire led to the rededication of the Second Temple and the establishment of the Hasmonean dynasty. This event is traditionally dated to 167-160 BCE.",
      "date": "-0167"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Destruction of the Second Temple",
      "text": "The Second Temple was destroyed by the Romans in 70 CE, a pivotal event in Jewish history that led to the Jewish diaspora.",
      "date": "0070"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Compilation of the Mishnah",
      "text": "The Mishnah, the first major written redaction of the Jewish oral traditions known as the Oral Torah, was compiled around 200 CE.",
      "date": "0200"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of the Talmud",
      "text": "The Talmud, a central text of Rabbinic Judaism consisting of the Mishnah and the Gemara, was completed around 500 CE.",
