      "headline": "Formation of the National League",
      "text": "The National League of Professional Baseball Clubs, known simply as the National League (NL), was formed on February 2, 1876. It was the first professional baseball league in the United States.",
      "date": "1876-02-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the American League",
      "text": "The American League (AL) was established as a major league in 1901, originally formed as the Western League in 1893 before changing its name.",
      "date": "1901"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First World Series",
      "text": "The first World Series was held in 1903, pitting the champions of the National League against the champions of the American League. The Boston Americans (later known as the Red Sox) defeated the Pittsburgh Pirates.",
      "date": "1903"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the Designated Hitter",
      "text": "The American League adopted the designated hitter rule in 1973, allowing teams to have one player, who does not play a defensive position, bat in place of the pitcher.",
      "date": "1973"
    },
    {
      "headline": "MLB Expansion",
      "text": "Major League Baseball expanded several times, notably in 1961 and 1962, adding teams such as the Los Angeles Angels and the New York Mets. Further expansions occurred in 1969, 1977, 1993, and 1998.",
      "date": "1961"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Interleague Play Introduced",
      "text": "In 1997, MLB introduced interleague play, allowing teams from the American League and National League to compete against each other during the regular season.",
      "date": "1997"
    },
    {
      "headline": "MLB Advanced Media Founded",
      "text": "MLB Advanced Media, the digital arm of Major League Baseball, was founded in 2000 to manage the league's online and interactive media ventures.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Houston Astros Move to the American League",
      "text": "In 2013, the Houston Astros moved from the National League Central division to the American League West division, balancing the leagues with 15 teams each.",
      "date": "2013"
    },
