      "text": "The Continental Marines were disbanded in 1783 following the end of the American Revolutionary War.",
      "date": "1783"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reestablishment as the United States Marine Corps",
      "text": "The United States Marine Corps was formally reestablished on July 11, 1798, by an act of Congress.",
      "date": "1798-07-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Barbary Wars",
      "text": "The Marines played a significant role in the First Barbary War (1801-1805), including the notable Battle of Derna in 1805.",
      "date": "1805"
    },
    {
      "headline": "War of 1812",
      "text": "During the War of 1812, the Marines participated in several key battles, including the defense of Washington, D.C., and the Battle of New Orleans in 1815.",
      "date": "1815"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mexican-American War",
      "text": "The Marines were involved in the Mexican-American War (1846-1848), participating in the capture of Mexico City in 1847.",
      "date": "1847"
    },
    {
      "headline": "American Civil War",
      "text": "The Marines served in the American Civil War (1861-1865), participating in both land and naval engagements.",
      "date": "1865"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Spanish-American War",
      "text": "In 1898, the Marines participated in the Spanish-American War, notably in the Battle of Guantánamo Bay.",
      "date": "1898"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World War I",
      "text": "The Marines played a crucial role in World War I, particularly in the Battle of Belleau Wood in 1918.",
      "date": "1918"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World War II",
      "text": "During World War II (1939-1945), the Marines were instrumental in the Pacific Theater, participating in major battles such as Iwo Jima and Okinawa.",
      "date": "1945"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Korean War",
      "text": "The Marines were heavily involved in the Korean War (1950-1953), including the Inchon Landing and the Battle of Chosin Reservoir.",
      "date": "1953"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Vietnam War",
      "text": "The Marine Corps played a significant role in the Vietnam War (1955-1975), with major operations such as the Battle of Khe Sanh.",
