      "headline": "Kangxi Emperor's Reign Begins",
      "text": "The Kangxi Emperor began his reign in 1661, which lasted until 1722. His reign is noted for consolidation of power and territorial expansion.",
      "date": "1661"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Qianlong Emperor's Reign",
      "text": "The Qianlong Emperor reigned from 1735 to 1796, during which the Qing dynasty reached its height in terms of territorial expansion and cultural achievements.",
      "date": "1735"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Opium Wars",
      "text": "The First Opium War (1839-1842) and the Second Opium War (1856-1860) marked significant conflicts between the Qing dynasty and Western powers, leading to significant territorial and economic concessions.",
      "date": "1839"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Taiping Rebellion",
      "text": "The Taiping Rebellion (1850-1864) was a massive civil war in southern China against the ruling Qing dynasty, led by Hong Xiuquan.",
      "date": "1850"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Boxer Rebellion",
      "text": "The Boxer Rebellion (1899-1901) was an anti-foreign, anti-colonial, and anti-Christian uprising in China, which was eventually suppressed by an Eight-Nation Alliance.",
      "date": "1899"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Xinhai Revolution",
      "text": "The Xinhai Revolution began in October 1911, leading to the abdication of the last Qing emperor, Puyi, in February 1912, marking the end of the Qing dynasty.",
      "date": "1911-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Abdication of the Last Emperor",
