      "text": "According to Aztec legend, Tenochtitlan was founded on March 13, 1325, when the Mexicas saw an eagle perched on a cactus, eating a snake.",
      "date": "1325-03-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Spanish Conquest of Tenochtitlan",
      "text": "On August 13, 1521, Spanish conquistadors led by Hernán Cortés, along with their indigenous allies, captured Tenochtitlan, marking the fall of the Aztec Empire.",
      "date": "1521-08-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of Mexico City",
      "text": "Following the conquest, Mexico City was established by the Spanish on the ruins of Tenochtitlan in 1524, becoming the capital of the Viceroyalty of New Spain.",
      "date": "1524"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mexico City Becomes Capital of Independent Mexico",
      "text": "After Mexico gained independence from Spain in 1821, Mexico City was designated as the capital of the newly independent nation.",
      "date": "1821"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reform War and French Intervention",
      "text": "During the mid-19th century, Mexico City was a focal point during the Reform War (1857-1861) and the subsequent French Intervention (1861-1867).",
      "date": "1857"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mexican Revolution",
      "text": "Mexico City played a significant role during the Mexican Revolution (1910-1920), serving as a political and military center.",
      "date": "1910"
    },
    {
      "headline": "1957 Mexico City Earthquake",
      "text": "On July 28, 1957, a major earthquake struck Mexico City, causing significant damage and loss of life.",
      "date": "1957-07-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "1968 Summer Olympics",
      "text": "Mexico City hosted the 1968 Summer Olympics, marking the first time the event was held in Latin America.",
      "date": "1968"
    },
    {
      "headline": "1985 Mexico City Earthquake",
      "text": "On September 19, 1985, a devastating earthquake struck Mexico City, resulting in thousands of deaths and widespread destruction.",
      "date": "1985-09-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Political Reforms and Greater Autonomy",
      "text": "In 1997, political reforms granted Mexico City greater autonomy, allowing residents to elect their own mayor for the first time.",
      "date": "1997"
    },
    {
      "headline": "2017 Mexico City Earthquake",
      "text": "On September 19, 2017, another powerful earthquake struck Mexico City, coincidentally on the same date as the 1985 quake, causing significant damage and casualties.",
      "date": "2017-09-19"
    }
  ]
}

