      "headline": "Inception of the Barkley Marathons",
      "text": "The Barkley Marathons was conceptualized by Gary Cantrell (also known as 'Lazarus Lake') in 1986. The race was inspired by the 1977 escape of James Earl Ray, the assassin of Martin Luther King Jr., from Brushy Mountain State Penitentiary, which is near the race's location.",
      "date": "1986"
