      "headline": "British Naval Task Force Dispatched",
      "text": "On 5 April 1982, the British government dispatched a naval task force to engage the Argentine Navy and Air Force and prepare for an amphibious assault on the islands.",
      "date": "1982-04-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sinking of ARA General Belgrano",
      "text": "On 2 May 1982, the British submarine HMS Conqueror sank the Argentine cruiser ARA General Belgrano, resulting in significant Argentine casualties.",
      "date": "1982-05-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Goose Green",
      "text": "The Battle of Goose Green took place from 28 to 29 May 1982, resulting in a British victory and the capture of Argentine forces.",
      "date": "1982-05-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "British Forces Land at San Carlos",
      "text": "On 21 May 1982, British forces made an amphibious landing at San Carlos on East Falkland, establishing a beachhead.",
      "date": "1982-05-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Mount Tumbledown",
      "text": "The Battle of Mount Tumbledown occurred on 13 June 1982, with British forces capturing the strategic position from Argentine defenders.",
      "date": "1982-06-13"
    },
