      "text": "On January 3, 2009, Satoshi Nakamoto mined the first block of the Bitcoin blockchain, known as the 'Genesis Block' or 'Block 0'. This block contained a reward of 50 bitcoins.",
      "date": "2009-01-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Last Known Communication",
      "text": "In December 2010, Satoshi Nakamoto handed over control of the Bitcoin repository and network alert key to Gavin Andresen and transferred several related domains to various prominent members of the Bitcoin community. This marked Nakamoto's last known communication.",
