      "text": "In August 1975, East Germany signed the Helsinki Accords, which were part of an effort to improve relations between the Communist bloc and the West.",
      "date": "1975-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mass Emigration and Protests",
      "text": "In 1989, mass emigration through Hungary and Czechoslovakia and widespread protests in East Germany led to political changes.",
      "date": "1989"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fall of the Berlin Wall",
      "text": "On 9 November 1989, the Berlin Wall fell, marking the beginning of the end for East Germany and leading to the reunification of Germany.",
