      "headline": "Original Pantheon Commissioned",
      "text": "The original Pantheon was commissioned by Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa during the reign of Augustus. The exact date of its commissioning is not specified, but it was part of Agrippa's building projects in Rome.",
      "date": "-0027"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Original Pantheon Destroyed by Fire",
      "text": "The original Pantheon was destroyed by fire in 80 AD. This fire was part of a larger conflagration that affected much of Rome.",
      "date": "0080"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reconstruction by Domitian",
      "text": "The Pantheon was rebuilt by Emperor Domitian after the fire of 80 AD. However, this structure was also destroyed, possibly by lightning.",
      "date": "0081"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Current Pantheon Construction Ordered by Hadrian",
      "text": "The current Pantheon was ordered by Emperor Hadrian and probably dedicated around 126 AD. Hadrian chose to retain the inscription of Agrippa's older temple on the new building.",
      "date": "0126"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Pantheon Converted to a Christian Church",
      "text": "In 609 AD, the Pantheon was consecrated as a Christian church by Pope Boniface IV, dedicated to St. Mary and the Martyrs. This conversion helped preserve the building through the centuries.",
      "date": "0609"
    }
  ]
}

