      "headline": "Formation of Delta Force",
      "text": "Delta Force was officially established in November 1977 by Colonel Charles Beckwith, following his experiences with the British Special Air Service (SAS).",
      "date": "1977-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Eagle Claw",
      "text": "In April 1980, Delta Force participated in Operation Eagle Claw, an attempt to rescue American hostages held in Tehran, Iran. The mission was aborted after a helicopter crash, resulting in the deaths of eight servicemen.",
      "date": "1980-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Urgent Fury",
      "text": "In October 1983, Delta Force took part in Operation Urgent Fury, the U.S. invasion of Grenada, to rescue American medical students and restore order.",
      "date": "1983-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Just Cause",
      "text": "Delta Force was involved in Operation Just Cause in December 1989, the U.S. invasion of Panama, which aimed to depose Panamanian leader Manuel Noriega.",
      "date": "1989-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Gothic Serpent",
      "text": "In 1993, Delta Force participated in Operation Gothic Serpent in Somalia, which included the Battle of Mogadishu in October, aiming to capture warlord Mohamed Farrah Aidid.",
      "date": "1993-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Enduring Freedom",
      "text": "Following the September 11 attacks in 2001, Delta Force was deployed to Afghanistan as part of Operation Enduring Freedom to dismantle al-Qaeda and remove the Taliban from power.",
      "date": "2001"
    },
