      "text": "The first Ironman Triathlon was held on February 18, 1978, in Oahu, Hawaii. It was conceived by U.S. Navy Commander John Collins and his wife, Judy, as a way to challenge athletes to complete a race combining the Waikiki Roughwater Swim, the Around-Oahu Bike Race, and the Honolulu Marathon.",
