      "text": "Emmett Till's funeral was held on September 3, 1955, in Chicago. His mother, Mamie Till-Mobley, insisted on an open casket to show the world the brutality of his murder.",
      "date": "1955-09-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Trial of Roy Bryant and J.W. Milam",
      "text": "The trial of Roy Bryant and J.W. Milam began on September 19, 1955, in Sumner, Mississippi. They were acquitted by an all-white jury on September 23, 1955.",
      "date": "1955-09-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Acquittal of Killers",
      "text": "On September 23, 1955, Roy Bryant and J.W. Milam were acquitted of Emmett Till's murder.",
      "date": "1955-09-23"
    },
