      "text": "Harald Sigurdsson, later known as Harald Hardrada, was born in 1015 in Norway.",
      "date": "1015"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Stiklestad",
      "text": "In 1030, Harald fought in the Battle of Stiklestad alongside his half-brother Olaf II of Norway, who was killed in the battle.",
      "date": "1030"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exile and Service in Kievan Rus'",
      "text": "After the Battle of Stiklestad, Harald fled to Kievan Rus', where he served as a military commander under Grand Prince Yaroslav the Wise.",
      "date": "1030"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Service in the Byzantine Empire",
      "text": "Around 1034, Harald traveled to Constantinople and joined the Varangian Guard, serving as a chief military commander.",
      "date": "1034"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return to Norway",
      "text": "In 1045, Harald returned to Norway and claimed the throne, becoming co-king with Magnus the Good.",
      "date": "1045"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sole King of Norway",
      "text": "In 1047, following the death of Magnus the Good, Harald became the sole King of Norway.",
      "date": "1047"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Conflict with Denmark",
      "text": "Harald claimed the Danish throne and engaged in a series of conflicts with King Sweyn II of Denmark until 1064.",
      "date": "1047"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Peace Treaty with Denmark",
      "text": "In 1064, Harald and Sweyn II of Denmark agreed to a peace treaty, ending Harald's claim to the Danish throne.",
      "date": "1064"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Invasion of England",
      "text": "In 1066, Harald invaded England, claiming the English throne. He was defeated and killed at the Battle of Stamford Bridge.",
      "date": "1066-09-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Harald Hardrada",
      "text": "Harald Hardrada died on September 25, 1066, at the Battle of Stamford Bridge in England.",
      "date": "1066-09-25"
    }
  ]
}

