      "text": "In 1913, Niels Bohr introduced a model of the atom that incorporated quantum theory, explaining how electrons can have stable orbits around the nucleus.",
      "date": "1913"
    },
    {
      "headline": "De Broglie's Matter Waves",
      "text": "In 1924, Louis de Broglie proposed that particles, such as electrons, exhibit wave-like properties, introducing the concept of matter waves.",
      "date": "1924"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Heisenberg's Uncertainty Principle",
      "text": "In 1927, Werner Heisenberg formulated the uncertainty principle, stating that the position and momentum of a particle cannot both be precisely determined at the same time.",
      "date": "1927"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Schrödinger's Wave Equation",
      "text": "In 1926, Erwin Schrödinger developed the wave equation, which describes how the quantum state of a physical system changes over time.",
      "date": "1926"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dirac's Relativistic Quantum Mechanics",
      "text": "In 1928, Paul Dirac formulated a relativistic version of quantum mechanics, predicting the existence of antimatter.",
      "date": "1928"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Discovery of Quantum Entanglement",
      "text": "In 1935, Albert Einstein, Boris Podolsky, and Nathan Rosen published a paper describing quantum entanglement, a phenomenon where particles become interconnected and the state of one instantly influences the state of another, regardless of distance.",
      "date": "1935"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Quantum Field Theory",
      "text": "In the 1940s, quantum field theory was developed, combining quantum mechanics with special relativity to describe the behavior of fields and particles.",
      "date": "1940"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bell's Theorem",
      "text": "In 1964, John Bell formulated Bell's theorem, which showed that certain predictions of quantum mechanics are incompatible with local hidden variable theories.",
      "date": "1964"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Quantum Information Science",
      "text": "In the late 20th century, quantum information science emerged, exploring the use of quantum mechanics for information processing, including quantum computing and quantum cryptography.",
      "date": "1980"
    }
  ]
}

