      "text": "In 1874, French neurologist Jean-Martin Charcot identified and named the disease amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS).",
      "date": "1874"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lou Gehrig Diagnosed with ALS",
      "text": "In 1939, famous baseball player Lou Gehrig was diagnosed with ALS, bringing significant public attention to the disease.",
      "date": "1939"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Discovery of SOD1 Gene Mutation",
      "text": "In 1993, researchers discovered that mutations in the SOD1 gene are linked to some cases of familial ALS.",
      "date": "1993"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Approval of Riluzole",
      "text": "In 1995, the FDA approved Riluzole, the first drug treatment for ALS, which can extend survival by a few months.",
      "date": "1995"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ice Bucket Challenge",
      "text": "In 2014, the Ice Bucket Challenge went viral on social media, raising awareness and over $115 million for ALS research.",
      "date": "2014"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Approval of Edaravone",
      "text": "In 2017, the FDA approved Edaravone, a drug that may slow the decline of physical function in ALS patients.",
      "date": "2017"
    }
  ]
}

