      "text": "On January 6, 2021, the United States Capitol Building in Washington, D.C., was attacked by a mob of supporters of then-president Donald Trump. The attack was an attempt to prevent Congress from certifying the Electoral College votes for President-elect Joe Biden.",
      "date": "2021-01-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Ashli Babbitt",
      "text": "During the storming of the Capitol on January 6, 2021, Ashli Babbitt was shot by Capitol Police while attempting to breach a barricaded door. She later died from her injuries.",
      "date": "2021-01-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Brian Sicknick",
      "text": "Capitol Police officer Brian Sicknick died on January 7, 2021, from natural causes after being assaulted by rioters during the Capitol attack.",
      "date": "2021-01-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Certification of Electoral College Results",
      "text": "Despite the attack, Congress reconvened later on January 6, 2021, and certified the Electoral College results, confirming Joe Biden's victory in the 2020 presidential election.",
      "date": "2021-01-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Deaths by Suicide of Responding Officers",
      "text": "Within seven months following the attack, four officers who responded to the Capitol attack died by suicide.",
      "date": "2021-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Financial Damage Assessment",
      "text": "The damage caused by the attackers during the storming of the Capitol was assessed to exceed $2.7 million.",
      "date": "2021"
    }
  ]
}

