      "headline": "Birth of Mustafa Kemal Atatürk",
      "text": "Mustafa Kemal Atatürk was born on May 19, 1881, in Salonica, then part of the Ottoman Empire (now Thessaloniki, Greece).",
      "date": "1881-05-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Graduation from Military Academy",
      "text": "In 1905, Mustafa Kemal graduated from the Ottoman Military Academy in Istanbul as a staff captain.",
      "date": "1905"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Role in the Young Turk Revolution",
      "text": "In 1908, Mustafa Kemal played a role in the Young Turk Revolution, which restored the Ottoman constitution and parliament.",
      "date": "1908"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Participation in the Italo-Turkish War",
      "text": "Mustafa Kemal served in the Italo-Turkish War in 1911-1912, where he gained valuable military experience.",
      "date": "1911"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Gallipoli Campaign",
      "text": "In 1915, Mustafa Kemal played a crucial role in the defense of the Gallipoli Peninsula during World War I, which earned him national recognition.",
      "date": "1915"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Appointed as Commander of the Seventh Army",
      "text": "In 1917, Mustafa Kemal was appointed as the commander of the Seventh Army in Palestine.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Armistice of Mudros",
      "text": "On October 30, 1918, the Armistice of Mudros was signed, marking the end of Ottoman participation in World War I.",
      "date": "1918-10-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Arrival in Samsun",
      "text": "On May 19, 1919, Mustafa Kemal arrived in Samsun, marking the beginning of the Turkish War of Independence.",
      "date": "1919-05-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the Grand National Assembly",
      "text": "On April 23, 1920, Mustafa Kemal established the Grand National Assembly in Ankara, which became the new government of Turkey.",
      "date": "1920-04-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Sakarya",
      "text": "In August-September 1921, Mustafa Kemal led Turkish forces to victory in the Battle of Sakarya, a turning point in the War of Independence.",
      "date": "1921-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Proclamation of the Republic of Turkey",
      "text": "On October 29, 1923, Mustafa Kemal proclaimed the Republic of Turkey and became its first president.",
      "date": "1923-10-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Adoption of the Surname 'Atatürk'",
      "text": "In 1934, Mustafa Kemal was given the surname 'Atatürk', meaning 'Father of the Turks', following the Surname Law.",
      "date": "1934"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Mustafa Kemal Atatürk",
      "text": "Mustafa Kemal Atatürk died on November 10, 1938, in Istanbul, Turkey.",
